<title>USA: First Union Real Estate sets credit line.</title>
<headline>First Union Real Estate sets credit line.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Union Real Estate Investments said on Thursday it signed a $96 million revolving credit facility with a syndicate of four banks led by National City Bank of Cleveland as administrative agent.</p>
<p>The new credit facility has a two-year term and can be extended at the end of each year for an additional year at the request of the company and upon consent of the bank group, First Union said.</p>
</text>
